members.member:
Gets the unique identifier for the record.
The unique identifier value in string type. The default value is null.
/// The unique identifier is used to differentiate one record from another. It should be a string that is unique across all records in the datasource.

member.example:

This example demonstrates how to programmatically replace the  and control whether to reset or preserve query states. 

<button @onclick="() => ReloadDataAsync(preserveState: true)">UpdateTreeGridDataSource</button> 

<SfTreeGrid @ref="MyTreeGrid" DataSource="@TreeItems"> 
    <TreeGridColumns> 
        <TreeGridColumn Field="Name" HeaderText="Name"></TreeGridColumn> 
        <TreeGridColumn Field="Category" HeaderText="Category"></TreeGridColumn> 
    </TreeGridColumns> 
</SfTreeGrid> 

@code { 
    SfTreeGrid<MyModel> MyTreeGrid; 
    List<MyModel> TreeItems = new List<MyModel>(); 

    private async Task ReloadDataAsync(bool preserveState) 
    { 
        // Load fresh data from API or database 
        TreeItems = await LoadDataFromApiAsync(); 

        // Update TreeGrid with new data 
        await MyTreeGrid.RefreshDataAsync(preserveState); 
    } 
}

The following example demonstrates how to use the ScrollIntoViewAsync method to scroll to a specific row or column in a Blazor Tree Grid:

<button id="ScrollIntoView" @onclick="Scroll">ScrollIntoView</button>
<SfTreeGrid @ref="treegrid" DataSource="@Orders">
 ........
</SfTreeGrid>
@code{
   SfTreeGrid<Order> treegrid;
   private async Task Scroll()
   {
       await treegrid.ScrollIntoViewAsync(2, 3);
   }
}

